---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="electronics"
  title="MOSFET & CMOS Logic"
  description="A plate of metal over an insulator, close enough to a slab of silicon to pull a conducting layer into existence underneath it. Nothing crosses the insulator, so the control costs no current at all, and that is the whole reason a chip can hold billions of these. Wire a p-type one above an n-type one and you have an inverter that draws power only while it is changing its mind."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="mos" width="1040" height="620"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>View</label>
        <div class="seg" id="view">
          <button data-v="device" class="active">The device</button>
          <button data-v="gate">The logic gate</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dev-only">
        <div class="control">
          <label>Type</label>
          <div class="seg" id="type">
            <button data-t="n" class="active">nMOS</button>
            <button data-t="p">pMOS</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label>Curve</label>
          <div class="seg" id="curve">
            <button data-c="out" class="active">Output</button>
            <button data-c="xfer">Transfer</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label><span id="vgslab">Gate voltage V_GS</span> <b id="vgsval">—</b></label>
          <input type="range" id="vgs" min="0" max="500" step="1" value="200" />
          <div class="scale-hint"><span>no channel</span><span>wide open</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label><span id="vdslab">Drain voltage V_DS</span> <b id="vdsval">—</b></label>
          <input type="range" id="vds" min="0" max="500" step="1" value="120" />
          <div class="scale-hint"><span>a plain resistor</span><span>pinched off</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label>Threshold V_th <b id="vthval">—</b></label>
          <input type="range" id="vth" min="20" max="250" step="1" value="100" />
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label>Width over length W/L <b id="wlval">—</b></label>
          <input type="range" id="wl" min="10" max="400" step="5" value="100" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="gate-only" hidden>
        <div class="control">
          <label>Gate</label>
          <div class="seg" id="gate">
            <button data-g="inv" class="active">NOT</button>
            <button data-g="nand">NAND</button>
            <button data-g="nor">NOR</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label>Inputs</label>
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="ina" /> A is high</label>
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="inb" /> B is high</label>
        </div>

        <div class="control" id="ctl-vin">
          <label>Or sweep A by hand <b id="vinval">—</b></label>
          <input type="range" id="vin" min="0" max="500" step="1" value="0" />
          <div class="scale-hint"><span>0 V</span><span>V_DD</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label>Supply V_DD <b id="vddval">—</b></label>
          <input type="range" id="vdd" min="100" max="500" step="5" value="300" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">—</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">—</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">—</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">—</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">—</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l6">—</span><b id="r6">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l7">—</span><b id="r7">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        In the gate view you can click the input labels on the schematic as well
        as the boxes here. The green wire is the one actually conducting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Start with the gate voltage at zero. Source and drain are two n-type
      islands in a p-type sea, so whichever way you push, one of the two
      junctions is <b>backwards</b> and nothing flows. A MOSFET with no gate
      voltage is not a bad conductor, it is two diodes back to back.
    </li>
    <li>
      Raise the gate. Nothing crosses the oxide, but the field through it drives
      holes away and, past <b>V_th</b>, pulls enough electrons up against the
      underside of the insulator to <b>invert</b> that layer into n-type. A
      conducting bridge appears between source and drain that was not there a
      moment ago, made of carriers borrowed from the substrate.
    </li>
    <li>
      With the drain voltage small, the channel is an even sheet and the device
      is an honest <b>resistor whose value you set with the gate</b>. That is
      the triode region, and it is why a MOSFET makes a good switch: fully on,
      it is just a small resistance.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now raise the drain. The channel is thinner at the drain end, because what
      holds it open there is V_GS − V(x), and V(x) has climbed. Push until
      V_DS = V_GS − V_th and the channel <b>pinches off</b> at the drain. Past
      that, extra drain voltage falls across the pinched gap instead of the
      channel, the current stops growing, and the device becomes a
      <b>current source controlled by the gate</b>. Watch the carriers speed up
      as the channel narrows: same current, less room.
    </li>
    <li>
      Look at the <b>shape of the channel</b> itself. Current is the same at
      every point along it, so where the layer is thinner the carriers must move
      faster, and you can see them do it. The taper is not a decoration, it
      <b>is</b> the reason the saturation current goes as the square of the
      overdrive.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch to <b>the logic gate</b>. The p-type transistor turns on when its
      gate is <b>low</b> and the n-type when it is <b>high</b>, so exactly one
      of them conducts. The output is either tied hard to the supply or hard to
      ground, never both and never neither, which is what makes the levels
      restore themselves instead of degrading down a chain.
    </li>
    <li>
      Sweep the input by hand and watch the supply current. It is essentially
      <b>zero at both ends</b> and spikes only in the middle of the transition,
      where both transistors are briefly on together. That single fact is why
      CMOS won: a circuit that is not switching costs almost nothing, so you can
      afford to put billions of them on one piece of silicon.
    </li>
    <li>
      Try NAND and NOR. The pull-down network is the logic you want and the
      pull-up is its <b>dual</b>: series where the other is parallel. Two nMOS
      in series conduct only when both inputs are high, so the output only falls
      then, which is NAND. Nobody had to design the top half separately.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The square-law MOSFET, drawn where it happens. The gate is one plate of a
  // capacitor and the silicon under the oxide is the other, so gate voltage
  // buys charge, and past threshold that charge is a conducting channel:
  //
  //     cutoff       V_GS < V_th                 I_D = 0
  //     triode       V_DS < V_GS - V_th          I_D = k(V_ov V_DS - V_DS²/2)
  //     saturation   V_DS > V_GS - V_th          I_D = k V_ov² / 2
  //
  // The same model, run twice with the signs swapped, is a CMOS gate.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  const state = {
    view: 'device' as 'device' | 'gate',
    type: 'n' as 'n' | 'p',
    curve: 'out' as 'out' | 'xfer',
    vgs: 2,
    vds: 1.2,
    vth: 1,
    wl: 1,
    gate: 'inv' as 'inv' | 'nand' | 'nor',
    a: false,
    b: false,
    vin: 0,
    vdd: 3,
    running: true,
  };

  const KP = 2e-3; // A/V² at W/L = 1

  /** Square-law drain current, everything in magnitudes. */
  function idOf(vgs: number, vds: number, vth = state.vth, wl = state.wl) {
    const ov = vgs - vth;
    if (ov <= 0 || vds <= 0) return 0;
    const k = KP * wl;
    return vds < ov ? k * (ov * vds - (vds * vds) / 2) : (k * ov * ov) / 2;
  }
  const ov = () => state.vgs - state.vth;
  const regime = () => (ov() <= 0 ? 'cutoff' : state.vds < ov() ? 'triode' : 'saturation');

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('mos') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssv = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${cssv('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236'},${a})`;
  const bg = () => cssv('--stage-bg') || '#0d0e12';
  const { label } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const ACC = '#7c8cff'; // gate, and the field it makes
  const TEAL = '#5eead4'; // electrons, and the channel
  const WARM = '#f59e0b'; // holes, and a high level
  const GREEN = '#34d399'; // current
  const HOT = '#f9736a';

  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w - rad, y);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y + h, x + w - rad, y + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x + rad, y + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y + h, x, y + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x + rad, y);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  type Box = { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number };
  function panel(p: Box, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }
  function eng(v: number, unit: string, digits = 2): string {
    const a = Math.abs(v);
    if (a === 0) return `0 ${unit}`;
    const steps: [number, string][] = [
      [1e-12, 'p'], [1e-9, 'n'], [1e-6, 'µ'], [1e-3, 'm'], [1, ''], [1e3, 'k'],
    ];
    let pick = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (a >= s[0]) pick = s;
    return `${(v / pick[0]).toFixed(digits)} ${pick[1]}${unit}`;
  }

  // ===========================================================================
  // THE DEVICE
  // ===========================================================================

  // The cross-section is the scene; one characteristic curve sits beside it,
  // and the side panel picks which of the two.
  const CROSS: Box = { x: 20, y: 74, w: 660, h: 460 };
  const PLOT: Box = { x: 700, y: 74, w: 320, h: 460 };
  const OUT = PLOT, XFER = PLOT;

  /** How much charge is left in the channel a fraction u of the way along. */
  function channelCharge(u: number) {
    const o = ov();
    if (o <= 0) return 0;
    const vd = Math.min(state.vds, o);
    const inner = o * o - (2 * o * vd - vd * vd) * u;
    return Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, inner)) / o; // 1 at the source, 0 when pinched
  }
  /** Where the channel gives out, as a fraction of the length. */
  function pinchAt() {
    if (state.vds <= ov() || ov() <= 0) return 1;
    // the excess drain voltage is dropped across a short depleted stretch
    return Math.max(0.55, 1 - 0.22 * (1 - ov() / state.vds));
  }
  /** Charge left at a fraction s of the way from source to drain. */
  function chQ(s: number) {
    if (ov() <= 0) return 0;
    const p = pinchAt();
    return s >= p ? 0 : channelCharge(s / p);
  }

  type Carrier = { u: number; v: number };
  let carriers: Carrier[] = [];
  const rnd = (() => {
    let s = 20260815;
    return () => ((s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0) / 4294967296);
  })();

  function seedCarriers() {
    carriers = [];
    for (let k = 0; k < 90; k++) carriers.push({ u: rnd(), v: rnd() });
  }

  function moveCarriers(dt: number) {
    const id = idOf(state.vgs, state.vds);
    if (id <= 0) return;
    for (const c of carriers) {
      // constant current with a tapering channel means the carriers have to
      // speed up exactly where there is less of them, and fly across the
      // pinched stretch where there are none at all
      const q = Math.max(0.1, chQ(c.u));
      c.u += (dt * (id / 4e-3) * 0.5) / q;
      if (c.u > 1) {
        c.u -= 1;
        c.v = rnd();
      }
    }
  }

  function drawCross() {
    panel(CROSS, state.type === 'n' ? 'AN n-CHANNEL MOSFET, IN CROSS SECTION' : 'A p-CHANNEL MOSFET, IN CROSS SECTION');
    const nType = state.type === 'n';
    const bulk = nType ? 'p-type substrate' : 'n-type substrate';
    const wells = nType ? 'n+' : 'p+';
    const carrierName = nType ? 'electrons' : 'holes';
    const carrierCol = nType ? TEAL : WARM;

    const x0 = CROSS.x + 90, x1 = CROSS.x + CROSS.w - 90;
    const top = CROSS.y + 150;
    const bot = CROSS.y + CROSS.h - 74;
    const sdW = 74;

    // the substrate
    ctx.fillStyle = nType ? 'rgba(245,158,11,0.06)' : 'rgba(94,234,212,0.06)';
    ctx.fillRect(x0, top, x1 - x0, bot - top);
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.2);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.strokeRect(x0, top, x1 - x0, bot - top);
    label(bulk, x1 - 8, bot - 10, 0.4, 'right', 11);

    // source and drain islands
    ctx.fillStyle = nType ? 'rgba(94,234,212,0.22)' : 'rgba(245,158,11,0.22)';
    ctx.fillRect(x0, top, sdW, 54);
    ctx.fillRect(x1 - sdW, top, sdW, 54);
    label(wells, x0 + 10, top + 20, 0.55, 'left', 11, carrierCol);
    label(wells, x1 - 10, top + 20, 0.55, 'right', 11, carrierCol);

    // the depletion region the gate pushes open under the oxide
    const depth = Math.min(46, Math.max(0, state.vgs / state.vth) * 16);
    if (depth > 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.2);
      ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x0 + sdW, top + depth);
      ctx.lineTo(x1 - sdW, top + depth);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(
        'depleted: the holes have been pushed away',
        (x0 + x1) / 2,
        top + depth + 16,
        0.32,
        'center',
        10
      );
    }

    // the oxide and the gate: a capacitor with silicon as its lower plate
    const oxT = top - 12;
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(124,140,255,0.14)';
    ctx.fillRect(x0 + sdW - 8, oxT, x1 - x0 - 2 * sdW + 16, 12);
    label('oxide, an insulator: nothing crosses it', x0 + sdW, oxT - 26, 0.32, 'left', 10);
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.3);
    ctx.fillRect(x0 + sdW - 14, oxT - 22, x1 - x0 - 2 * sdW + 28, 22);
    label('gate', (x0 + x1) / 2, oxT - 7, 0.85, 'center', 12);

    // the charge on the gate plate
    const nq = Math.min(11, Math.round((state.vgs / 5) * 11));
    for (let k = 0; k < nq; k++) {
      const gx = x0 + sdW + 6 + (k * (x1 - x0 - 2 * sdW - 12)) / Math.max(1, nq - 1);
      label(nType ? '+' : '−', gx, oxT - 26, 0.9, 'center', 12, ACC);
    }

    // the channel, if the gate has managed to make one
    const o = ov();
    const chL = x1 - sdW - (x0 + sdW);
    if (o > 0) {
      const pinch = pinchAt();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x0 + sdW, top);
      const N = 70;
      for (let k = 0; k <= N; k++) {
        const s = (k / N) * pinch;
        ctx.lineTo(x0 + sdW + s * chL, top + Math.max(1.5, chQ(s) * 22));
      }
      ctx.lineTo(x0 + sdW + pinch * chL, top);
      ctx.closePath();
      ctx.fillStyle = nType ? 'rgba(94,234,212,0.5)' : 'rgba(245,158,11,0.5)';
      ctx.fill();

      if (pinch < 0.999) {
        // the pinched stretch: no carriers left, all the extra voltage lands here
        ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(249,115,106,0.16)';
        ctx.fillRect(x0 + sdW + pinch * chL, top, (1 - pinch) * chL, 26);
        ctx.strokeStyle = HOT;
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
        ctx.setLineDash([3, 3]);
        ctx.strokeRect(x0 + sdW + pinch * chL, top, (1 - pinch) * chL, 26);
        ctx.setLineDash([]);
        label(
          'pinched off',
          x0 + sdW + (pinch + (1 - pinch) / 2) * chL,
          top - 6,
          0.9,
          'center',
          10.5,
          HOT
        );
      }

      // the carriers actually carrying the current
      for (const c of carriers) {
        const q = chQ(c.u);
        const cx = x0 + sdW + c.u * chL;
        const cy = top + 3 + c.v * Math.max(2, q * 19);
        ctx.fillStyle = carrierCol;
        ctx.globalAlpha = c.u > pinch ? 0.4 : 1;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(cx, cy, 2.6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      }
      label(
        `an inverted layer of ${carrierName}, borrowed from the substrate`,
        x0 + sdW,
        top + 44,
        0.45,
        'left',
        10.5,
        carrierCol
      );
    } else {
      label(
        'no channel: source and drain are two diodes back to back',
        (x0 + x1) / 2,
        top + 34,
        0.55,
        'center',
        11.5,
        HOT
      );
    }

    // terminals
    const term = (x: number, y: number, name: string, volts: string, col: string) => {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.4);
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x, y);
      ctx.lineTo(x, y - 34);
      ctx.stroke();
      label(name, x, y - 42, 0.85, 'center', 12, col);
      label(volts, x, y - 58, 0.95, 'center', 12, col);
    };
    term(x0 + sdW / 2, top, 'S', '0.00 V', inkA(0.7));
    term(x1 - sdW / 2, top, 'D', `${state.vds.toFixed(2)} V`, GREEN);
    term((x0 + x1) / 2, oxT - 22, 'G', `${state.vgs.toFixed(2)} V`, ACC);

    // the current, where it flows
    const id = idOf(state.vgs, state.vds);
    if (id > 1e-9) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      const ay = bot + 26;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x1 - sdW / 2, ay);
      ctx.lineTo(x0 + sdW / 2, ay);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x0 + sdW / 2, ay);
      ctx.lineTo(x0 + sdW / 2 + 9, ay - 4);
      ctx.lineTo(x0 + sdW / 2 + 9, ay + 4);
      ctx.closePath();
      ctx.fill();
      label(`I_D = ${eng(id, 'A')}`, (x0 + x1) / 2, ay + 18, 0.95, 'center', 12, GREEN);
    } else {
      label('no current at all', (x0 + x1) / 2, bot + 34, 0.5, 'center', 11);
    }
    // which of the three regimes it is, and the law that holds there
    const r = regime();
    const line =
      r === 'cutoff'
        ? 'cut off · I_D = 0'
        : r === 'triode'
          ? 'triode · I_D = k(V_ov·V_DS − V_DS²/2)'
          : 'saturation · I_D = k·V_ov²/2';
    label(line, CROSS.x + 14, CROSS.y + CROSS.h - 16, 0.85, 'left', 12.5, r === 'cutoff' ? HOT : TEAL);
  }

  // --- the two characteristic curves -----------------------------------------

  function drawOutput() {
    panel(OUT, 'DRAIN CURRENT AGAINST DRAIN VOLTAGE');
    const px = OUT.x + 52, py = OUT.y + 20, pw = OUT.w - 68, ph = OUT.h - 58;
    const VMAX = 5;
    const imax = Math.max(idOf(VMAX, VMAX), 1e-6) * 1.1;
    const X = (v: number) => px + (v / VMAX) * pw;
    const Y = (i: number) => py + ph - (i / imax) * ph;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('V_DS', px + pw, py + ph + 16, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('I_D', px - 8, py + 8, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label(eng(imax, 'A', 1), px - 8, py + 20, 0.3, 'right', 9);

    // a family of gate voltages, so the knob is visible as a family
    for (let g = 1; g <= 5; g++) {
      const vg = (g / 5) * VMAX;
      const on = Math.abs(vg - state.vgs) < 0.35;
      ctx.strokeStyle = on ? TEAL : inkA(0.22);
      ctx.lineWidth = on ? 2.4 : 1.2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let k = 0; k <= 120; k++) {
        const vd = (k / 120) * VMAX;
        const y = Y(idOf(vg, vd));
        k ? ctx.lineTo(X(vd), y) : ctx.moveTo(X(vd), y);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
      if (idOf(vg, VMAX) > imax * 0.04)
        label(`${vg.toFixed(1)}`, X(VMAX) - 2, Y(idOf(vg, VMAX)) - 5, on ? 0.9 : 0.35, 'right', 9.5, on ? TEAL : undefined);
    }

    // the parabola where the channel first pinches: the border between the two
    ctx.strokeStyle = HOT;
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let k = 0; k <= 80; k++) {
      const vd = (k / 80) * VMAX;
      const y = Y((KP * state.wl * vd * vd) / 2);
      k ? ctx.lineTo(X(vd), y) : ctx.moveTo(X(vd), y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label('V_DS = V_GS − V_th', px + 6, py + 14, 0.7, 'left', 10, HOT);
    label('triode', px + 12, py + ph - 12, 0.35, 'left', 10);
    label('saturation', px + pw - 6, py + ph - 12, 0.35, 'right', 10);

    ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(X(state.vds), Y(idOf(state.vgs, state.vds)), 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
  }

  function drawTransfer() {
    panel(XFER, 'DRAIN CURRENT AGAINST GATE VOLTAGE');
    const px = XFER.x + 52, py = XFER.y + 20, pw = XFER.w - 68, ph = XFER.h - 58;
    const VMAX = 5;
    const imax = Math.max(idOf(VMAX, state.vds), 1e-6) * 1.1;
    const X = (v: number) => px + (v / VMAX) * pw;
    const Y = (i: number) => py + ph - (i / imax) * ph;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('V_GS', px + pw, py + ph + 16, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('I_D', px - 8, py + 8, 0.35, 'right', 10);

    ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(X(state.vth), py);
    ctx.lineTo(X(state.vth), py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label('V_th', X(state.vth) + 5, py + 14, 0.8, 'left', 11, ACC);

    ctx.strokeStyle = TEAL;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let k = 0; k <= 160; k++) {
      const vg = (k / 160) * VMAX;
      const y = Y(idOf(vg, state.vds));
      k ? ctx.lineTo(X(vg), y) : ctx.moveTo(X(vg), y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(X(state.vgs), Y(idOf(state.vgs, state.vds)), 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    label(
      'flat until threshold, then a square law: nothing, then everything',
      px - 30,
      py + ph + 34,
      0.4,
      'left',
      10
    );
  }

  // ===========================================================================
  // THE LOGIC GATE
  // ===========================================================================

  const SCHEM: Box = { x: 20, y: 74, w: 480, h: 520 };
  const TRUTH: Box = { x: 530, y: 74, w: 490, h: 180 };
  // output voltage and supply current share one V_in axis in a single panel
  const VTC: Box = { x: 530, y: 292, w: 490, h: 302 };

  const VTHN = 0.8, VTHP = 0.8;
  const idn = (vgs: number, vds: number) => idOf(vgs, vds, VTHN, 1);
  const idp = (vsg: number, vsd: number) => idOf(vsg, vsd, VTHP, 1);

  /** Where the inverter's output settles for a given input, found by bisection. */
  function invOut(vin: number) {
    let lo = 0, hi = state.vdd;
    for (let k = 0; k < 46; k++) {
      const mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
      const f = idn(vin, mid) - idp(state.vdd - vin, state.vdd - mid);
      if (f > 0) hi = mid;
      else lo = mid;
    }
    return (lo + hi) / 2;
  }
  const invIdd = (vin: number) => idn(vin, invOut(vin));

  /** The analogue input, which the A checkbox simply snaps to a rail. */
  const vinNow = () => state.vin;

  function mos(x: number, y: number, type: 'p' | 'n', on: boolean, name: string) {
    const col = on ? GREEN : inkA(0.3);
    ctx.strokeStyle = col;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;
    // the gate plate and its lead
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x - 18, y - 15);
    ctx.lineTo(x - 18, y + 15);
    ctx.moveTo(x - 18, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x - (type === 'p' ? 30 : 26), y);
    ctx.stroke();
    if (type === 'p') {
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x - 34, y, 4.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    // the channel, and the two terminals coming off it
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x - 10, y - 15);
    ctx.lineTo(x - 10, y + 15);
    ctx.moveTo(x - 10, y - 11);
    ctx.lineTo(x + 12, y - 11);
    ctx.lineTo(x + 12, y - 26);
    ctx.moveTo(x - 10, y + 11);
    ctx.lineTo(x + 12, y + 11);
    ctx.lineTo(x + 12, y + 26);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(name, x + 22, y + 4, on ? 0.9 : 0.4, 'left', 11, on ? GREEN : undefined);
    label(type === 'p' ? 'p' : 'n', x - 4, y - 20, on ? 0.7 : 0.3, 'left', 10);
  }

  function wire(pts: [number, number][], on: boolean, lw = 2.2) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = on ? GREEN : inkA(0.28);
    ctx.lineWidth = on ? lw + 0.6 : lw;
    ctx.beginPath();
    pts.forEach(([x, y], k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y)));
    ctx.stroke();
  }

  function rail(y: number, x0: number, x1: number, name: string, col: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.45);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x0, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x1, y);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(name, x0 + 4, y - 9, 0.7, 'left', 12, col);
  }

  /** The far end of a transistor's gate lead, which is where its input wire meets it. */
  const leadX = (x: number, type: 'p' | 'n') => x - (type === 'p' ? 38 : 26);

  /** Where to click to flip an input. */
  let inputHits: { x: number; y: number; which: 'a' | 'b' }[] = [];

  function drawSchem() {
    panel(SCHEM, 'THE GATE, TRANSISTOR BY TRANSISTOR');
    inputHits = [];
    const cx = SCHEM.x + 280;
    const yT = SCHEM.y + 78, yB = SCHEM.y + SCHEM.h - 78;
    const outY = (yT + yB) / 2;
    rail(yT, SCHEM.x + 120, SCHEM.x + SCHEM.w - 50, 'V_DD', WARM);
    rail(yB, SCHEM.x + 120, SCHEM.x + SCHEM.w - 50, 'GND', ACC);

    const A = state.gate === 'inv' ? vinNow() > state.vdd / 2 : state.a;
    const B = state.b;
    const out =
      state.gate === 'inv' ? !A : state.gate === 'nand' ? !(A && B) : !(A || B);

    // A device is on when its own input says so: p-type on a low, n-type on a high.
    type Dev = { x: number; y: number; type: 'p' | 'n'; input: 'a' | 'b' };
    let devs: Dev[];
    let wires: [[number, number][], boolean][];

    if (state.gate === 'inv') {
      devs = [
        { x: cx, y: yT + 96, type: 'p', input: 'a' },
        { x: cx, y: yB - 96, type: 'n', input: 'a' },
      ];
      wires = [
        [[[cx + 12, yT + 70], [cx + 12, yT]], out],
        [[[cx + 12, yT + 122], [cx + 12, outY]], out],
        [[[cx + 12, outY], [cx + 12, yB - 122]], !out],
        [[[cx + 12, yB - 70], [cx + 12, yB]], !out],
      ];
    } else if (state.gate === 'nand') {
      // above: two in parallel, so either low input pulls the output up
      // below: two in series, so it only falls when both are high
      devs = [
        { x: cx - 62, y: yT + 96, type: 'p', input: 'a' },
        { x: cx + 86, y: yT + 96, type: 'p', input: 'b' },
        { x: cx, y: yB - 156, type: 'n', input: 'a' },
        { x: cx, y: yB - 74, type: 'n', input: 'b' },
      ];
      wires = [
        [[[cx - 50, yT + 70], [cx - 50, yT]], !A],
        [[[cx + 98, yT + 70], [cx + 98, yT]], !B],
        [[[cx - 50, yT + 122], [cx - 50, outY - 52], [cx + 98, outY - 52], [cx + 98, yT + 122]], out],
        [[[cx + 12, outY - 52], [cx + 12, outY]], out],
        [[[cx + 12, yB - 182], [cx + 12, outY]], !out],
        [[[cx + 12, yB - 130], [cx + 12, yB - 100]], A && B],
        [[[cx + 12, yB - 48], [cx + 12, yB]], !out],
      ];
    } else {
      // NOR is the mirror image: series above, parallel below
      devs = [
        { x: cx, y: yT + 74, type: 'p', input: 'a' },
        { x: cx, y: yT + 156, type: 'p', input: 'b' },
        { x: cx - 62, y: yB - 96, type: 'n', input: 'a' },
        { x: cx + 86, y: yB - 96, type: 'n', input: 'b' },
      ];
      wires = [
        [[[cx + 12, yT + 48], [cx + 12, yT]], out],
        [[[cx + 12, yT + 100], [cx + 12, yT + 130]], !A && !B],
        [[[cx + 12, yT + 182], [cx + 12, outY]], out],
        [[[cx - 50, yB - 122], [cx - 50, outY + 52], [cx + 98, outY + 52], [cx + 98, yB - 122]], !out],
        [[[cx + 12, outY + 52], [cx + 12, outY]], !out],
        [[[cx - 50, yB - 70], [cx - 50, yB]], A],
        [[[cx + 98, yB - 70], [cx + 98, yB]], B],
      ];
    }

    for (const [pts, on] of wires) wire(pts, on);
    for (const d of devs) {
      const high = d.input === 'a' ? A : B;
      const on = d.type === 'p' ? !high : high;
      mos(d.x, d.y, d.type, on, d.input.toUpperCase());
    }

    // the input buses, each running down the left and stubbing across to its gates
    const busX: Record<'a' | 'b', number> = { a: SCHEM.x + 44, b: SCHEM.x + 78 };
    const nodeY = SCHEM.y + 36;
    const used: ('a' | 'b')[] = state.gate === 'inv' ? ['a'] : ['a', 'b'];
    for (const which of used) {
      const mine = devs.filter((d) => d.input === which);
      const high = which === 'a' ? A : B;
      const col = high ? WARM : ACC;
      const bx = busX[which];
      ctx.strokeStyle = col;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.75;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(bx, nodeY);
      ctx.lineTo(bx, Math.max(...mine.map((d) => d.y)));
      for (const d of mine) {
        ctx.moveTo(bx, d.y);
        ctx.lineTo(leadX(d.x, d.type), d.y);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      for (const d of mine) {
        ctx.fillStyle = col;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(bx, d.y, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(bx, nodeY, 11, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      label(which.toUpperCase(), bx, nodeY + 5, 1, 'center', 12, bg());
      label(high ? '1' : '0', bx, nodeY - 17, 0.9, 'center', 11, col);
      inputHits.push({ x: bx, y: nodeY, which });
    }
    label('click to flip', busX.a - 12, nodeY + 30, 0.35, 'left', 10);

    // the output node
    const outVolts = state.gate === 'inv' ? invOut(vinNow()) : out ? state.vdd : 0;
    const outCol = outVolts > state.vdd / 2 ? WARM : ACC;
    wire([[cx + 12, outY], [cx + 150, outY]], true, 2.4);
    ctx.fillStyle = outCol;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(cx + 160, outY, 11, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    label(outVolts > state.vdd / 2 ? '1' : '0', cx + 160, outY + 5, 1, 'center', 13, bg());
    label('OUT', cx + 160, outY - 20, 0.8, 'center', 11, outCol);
    label(`${outVolts.toFixed(2)} V`, cx + 160, outY + 32, 0.9, 'center', 12, outCol);

    label(
      state.gate === 'inv'
        ? 'exactly one of the two is on, so the output is tied hard to a rail'
        : state.gate === 'nand'
          ? 'series below, parallel above: the top half is the dual of the bottom'
          : 'parallel below, series above: again the dual, and again for free',
      SCHEM.x + 16,
      SCHEM.y + SCHEM.h - 18,
      0.4,
      'left',
      10.5
    );
    label('the pull-up network', SCHEM.x + SCHEM.w - 16, yT + 24, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('the pull-down network', SCHEM.x + SCHEM.w - 16, yB - 16, 0.35, 'right', 10);
  }

  function drawTruth() {
    panel(TRUTH, 'WHAT IT DOES, IN FULL');
    const single = state.gate === 'inv';
    const A = single ? vinNow() > state.vdd / 2 : state.a;
    const B = state.b;
    const combine = (p: boolean, q: boolean) =>
      state.gate === 'nand' ? !(p && q) : !(p || q);
    const rows: [boolean, boolean, boolean][] = single
      ? [
          [false, false, true],
          [true, false, false],
        ]
      : [
          [false, false, combine(false, false)],
          [false, true, combine(false, true)],
          [true, false, combine(true, false)],
          [true, true, combine(true, true)],
        ];

    const x = TRUTH.x + 26;
    const y0 = TRUTH.y + 42;
    const colW = 54;
    label('A', x, y0 - 12, 0.4, 'center', 11);
    if (!single) label('B', x + colW, y0 - 12, 0.4, 'center', 11);
    label('OUT', x + colW * (single ? 1 : 2) + 6, y0 - 12, 0.4, 'center', 11);
    rows.forEach((r, k) => {
      const yy = y0 + 6 + k * 28;
      const here = r[0] === A && (single || r[1] === B);
      if (here) {
        ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(94,234,212,0.10)';
        rr(x - 22, yy - 18, colW * (single ? 2 : 3) + 40, 26, 6);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      label(r[0] ? '1' : '0', x, yy, here ? 1 : 0.4, 'center', 12, r[0] ? WARM : ACC);
      if (!single) label(r[1] ? '1' : '0', x + colW, yy, here ? 1 : 0.4, 'center', 12, r[1] ? WARM : ACC);
      label(r[2] ? '1' : '0', x + colW * (single ? 1 : 2) + 6, yy, here ? 1 : 0.4, 'center', 12, r[2] ? WARM : ACC);
    });
    label(
      state.gate === 'inv'
        ? 'the whole of NOT'
        : state.gate === 'nand'
          ? 'NAND alone can build every other gate there is'
          : 'NOR can too, on its own',
      TRUTH.x + TRUTH.w - 20,
      TRUTH.y + TRUTH.h - 18,
      0.4,
      'right',
      10.5
    );
  }

  /** V_out on top and the supply current under it, on one shared V_in axis. */
  function drawVTC() {
    panel(VTC, 'THE OUTPUT, AND WHAT IT COSTS THE SUPPLY');
    const px = VTC.x + 56, pw = VTC.w - 78;
    const py1 = VTC.y + 24, ph1 = 158; // V_out
    const py2 = py1 + ph1 + 30, ph2 = 64; // I_DD
    const X = (v: number) => px + (v / state.vdd) * pw;
    const Yv = (v: number) => py1 + ph1 - (v / state.vdd) * ph1;

    let imax = 1e-9;
    for (let k = 0; k <= 100; k++) imax = Math.max(imax, invIdd((k / 100) * state.vdd));
    imax *= 1.15;
    const Yi = (i: number) => py2 + ph2 - (i / imax) * ph2;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py1);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py1 + ph1);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py1 + ph1);
    ctx.moveTo(px, py2);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py2 + ph2);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py2 + ph2);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('V_out', px - 8, py1 + 8, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('V_DD', px - 8, Yv(state.vdd) + 12, 0.3, 'right', 9);
    label('I_DD', px - 8, py2 + 8, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('V_in', px + pw, py2 + ph2 + 16, 0.35, 'right', 10);

    // the transfer curve
    ctx.strokeStyle = TEAL;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let k = 0; k <= 150; k++) {
      const vin = (k / 150) * state.vdd;
      const y = Yv(invOut(vin));
      k ? ctx.lineTo(X(vin), y) : ctx.moveTo(X(vin), y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    // the current it draws, directly underneath the transition that causes it
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, Yi(0));
    for (let k = 0; k <= 200; k++) {
      const vin = (k / 200) * state.vdd;
      ctx.lineTo(X(vin), Yi(invIdd(vin)));
    }
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, Yi(0));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(249,115,106,0.16)';
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = HOT;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let k = 0; k <= 200; k++) {
      const vin = (k / 200) * state.vdd;
      const y = Yi(invIdd(vin));
      k ? ctx.lineTo(X(vin), y) : ctx.moveTo(X(vin), y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    const vin = vinNow();
    ctx.fillStyle = WARM;
    for (const y of [Yv(invOut(vin)), Yi(invIdd(vin))]) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(X(vin), y, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }
    label(
      'the current only flows where the output is mid-swing',
      px + pw,
      py2 - 8,
      0.45,
      'right',
      10,
      HOT
    );
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    el('r' + n).textContent = val;
  };
  function updateReadout() {
    if (state.view === 'device') {
      const id = idOf(state.vgs, state.vds);
      setRow(1, state.type === 'n' ? 'Gate V_GS' : 'Gate V_SG', state.vgs.toFixed(2) + ' V');
      setRow(2, state.type === 'n' ? 'Drain V_DS' : 'Source-drain V_SD', state.vds.toFixed(2) + ' V');
      setRow(3, 'Overdrive V_ov', ov().toFixed(2) + ' V');
      setRow(4, 'Region', regime());
      setRow(5, 'Drain current I_D', eng(id, 'A'));
      setRow(6, 'Channel resistance', id > 1e-9 ? eng(state.vds / id, 'Ω') : 'open circuit');
      setRow(7, 'Transconductance g_m', eng(KP * state.wl * Math.max(0, ov()), 'S'));
    } else {
      const vin = vinNow();
      const vout = state.gate === 'inv' ? invOut(vin) : null;
      const A = state.gate === 'inv' ? vin > state.vdd / 2 : state.a;
      const out =
        state.gate === 'inv' ? !A : state.gate === 'nand' ? !(A && state.b) : !(A || state.b);
      setRow(1, 'Gate', state.gate === 'inv' ? 'NOT' : state.gate.toUpperCase());
      setRow(2, 'A', A ? '1' : '0');
      setRow(3, 'B', state.gate === 'inv' ? '—' : state.b ? '1' : '0');
      setRow(4, 'Output', out ? '1' : '0');
      setRow(5, 'Output voltage', (vout ?? (out ? state.vdd : 0)).toFixed(3) + ' V');
      setRow(6, 'Supply current', state.gate === 'inv' ? eng(invIdd(vin), 'A') : 'about zero');
      setRow(7, 'Static power', state.gate === 'inv' ? eng(invIdd(vin) * state.vdd, 'W') : 'about zero');
    }
  }

  // --- frame -----------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label(state.view === 'device' ? 'MOSFET' : 'CMOS logic', 20, 30, 0.85, 'left', 14);
    if (state.view === 'device') {
      drawCross();
      if (state.curve === 'xfer') drawTransfer();
      else drawOutput();
    } else {
      drawSchem();
      drawTruth();
      drawVTC();
    }
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  function frame(now: number) {
    const dt = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, (now - last) / 1000));
    last = now;
    if (state.running && state.view === 'device') moveCarriers(dt);
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {
    seedCarriers();
  });

  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void) {
    const input = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const run = () => apply(+input.value);
    input.addEventListener('input', run);
    run();
  }
  bindRange('vgs', (n) => {
    state.vgs = n / 100;
    el('vgsval').textContent = `${state.vgs.toFixed(2)} V`;
  });
  bindRange('vds', (n) => {
    state.vds = n / 100;
    el('vdsval').textContent = `${state.vds.toFixed(2)} V`;
  });
  bindRange('vth', (n) => {
    state.vth = n / 100;
    el('vthval').textContent = `${state.vth.toFixed(2)} V`;
  });
  bindRange('wl', (n) => {
    state.wl = n / 100;
    el('wlval').textContent = `${state.wl.toFixed(2)}`;
  });
  bindRange('vin', (n) => {
    state.vin = n / 100;
    el('vinval').textContent = `${state.vin.toFixed(2)} V`;
    const box = document.getElementById('ina') as HTMLInputElement;
    box.checked = state.vin > state.vdd / 2;
    state.a = box.checked;
  });
  bindRange('vdd', (n) => {
    state.vdd = n / 100;
    el('vddval').textContent = `${state.vdd.toFixed(2)} V`;
  });

  const inA = document.getElementById('ina') as HTMLInputElement;
  const inB = document.getElementById('inb') as HTMLInputElement;
  inA.addEventListener('change', () => {
    state.a = inA.checked;
    state.vin = state.a ? state.vdd : 0;
    const s = document.getElementById('vin') as HTMLInputElement;
    s.value = String(Math.round(state.vin * 100));
    el('vinval').textContent = `${state.vin.toFixed(2)} V`;
  });
  inB.addEventListener('change', () => (state.b = inB.checked));

  function syncView() {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.dev-only').forEach((e) => (e.hidden = state.view !== 'device'));
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.gate-only').forEach((e) => (e.hidden = state.view !== 'gate'));
    el('ctl-vin').style.display = state.gate === 'inv' ? '' : 'none';
    el('vgslab').textContent = state.type === 'n' ? 'Gate voltage V_GS' : 'Gate voltage V_SG';
    el('vdslab').textContent = state.type === 'n' ? 'Drain voltage V_DS' : 'Source-drain V_SD';
  }

  el('view').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#view button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.view = btn.dataset.v as 'device' | 'gate';
    syncView();
  });
  el('curve').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#curve button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.curve = btn.dataset.c as 'out' | 'xfer';
  });
  el('type').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#type button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.type = btn.dataset.t as 'n' | 'p';
    syncView();
  });
  el('gate').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#gate button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.gate = btn.dataset.g as 'inv' | 'nand' | 'nor';
    syncView();
  });

  // clicking an input right on the schematic
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    if (state.view !== 'gate') return;
    const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    const x = ((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width) * W;
    const y = ((e.clientY - r.top) / r.height) * H;
    for (const hit of inputHits) {
      if (Math.hypot(x - hit.x, y - hit.y) < 18) {
        const box = hit.which === 'a' ? inA : inB;
        box.checked = !box.checked;
        box.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true }));
        return;
      }
    }
  });
  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
    if (state.view !== 'gate') {
      canvas.style.cursor = 'default';
      return;
    }
    const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    const x = ((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width) * W;
    const y = ((e.clientY - r.top) / r.height) * H;
    canvas.style.cursor = inputHits.some((h) => Math.hypot(x - h.x, y - h.y) < 18)
      ? 'pointer'
      : 'default';
  });

  seedCarriers();
  syncView();
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

